First bytes: 003 357 365 036 300 202 006 277. In hex that's 0x03 0xEF 0xF5 0x3E. That looks like the TF checkpoint magic string. I know the format starts with the four byte magic 0xEF 0xF5 0xFF 0x03, then a version number, and then a series of records. The very first two bytes 0x03 0xEF are part of that, so I am looking at the right structure.

I can't read the table of contents by eye from that dump. I need a small throwaway program to walk the records and list out every tensor name and where it sits. I will write that helper in C, run it, and use the result to build the real thing.

The bpe file is in the standard format. The header line is there and the pairs follow, which is all I need. The 256 byte values are implicitly defined by the ordering that the original code used. Once I have the list of tensors I can start pulling them in.

